    {
      "id": "claim_eac3f06648734d6087e1132180bc32ff",
      "statement": "TrainingSpine.run merge order: (1) names = callback_names_override if set else default_names; (2) forbidden_callbacks is applied post-merge — each name in the map is force-removed from the merged list with a rank_zero_info log line, so a YAML or --callbacks override cannot re-enable it; (3) forbidden_monitors rejects a callback_cfg.checkpoint.monitor_metric before resolution (raises ValueError after a rank_zero_info); (4) registry.resolve(names, callback_cfg) validates names and applies the per-name knob overrides from callback_cfg (the YAML callbacks: block + cfg merged into the named specs); (5) registry.build(specs, ctx) constructs the pl.Callback list with the runtime CallbackContext; (6) extra_callbacks (e.g. LatentX0MAE) are appended; (7) validate_monitor checks monitor_metric against the union of registry + module + extra logged_metrics; (8) if no ModelCheckpoint survives the merge, raise ValueError; (9) build_trainer(callbacks=callbacks) + trainer.fit.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/core.py#L42-L161",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:efe08ec6252b6a16192d4d7add0fbc143258f7b4cc0b23ea0a5d193c1ba37758:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c8a02641de41437b85b827c4684cf216",
      "statement": "The GRPO ControlNet path passes forbidden_callbacks={'fid': 'constant frozen-base metric'} and forbidden_monitors={'val/fid': ...} to TrainingSpine.run, so unconditional FID (whose module.sample() rollout ignores the trainable ControlNet and yields a constant frozen-base metric) cannot be silently re-added by a YAML or --callbacks override, and a checkpoint monitoring val/fid raises ValueError instead of silently resuming on a meaningless metric.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/core.py#L108-L131",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:baa9a087d3738075b46be0830580e8b61797158d76daabfd0edccac6f3d2955a:"
